{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50d61844-03e1-47e6-9599-4d79a818d07e","agentId":"a07e08770c1a3b00c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are modifying a CadQuery machine model (AUTOKITCH food line, HAT v3 → v3.4). Work ONLY in this build tree:\nB = C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\b3\\arastirma\\_uretec\nPython sources in B\\h3\\ and B\\ (run from B as cwd; read each file's docstring \"Çalıştır\" line for how to self-check, e.g. `python ob_calistir.py h3/h3_ray_ek_v1.py hizli`). World coords mm: x along the line, y up (floor = 0), z toward the corridor (machine front +79, back −830). The QR delivery cabinet (qr_cad_v1, unchanged module) stands across the robot corridor: x 4570–5430, z 670–1190, base plate y 16–21 on 17 mm levelling feet; its lower robot-side service door `servis_kapagi_alt` spans x 4572–5428, y 21–446, z 668–673. Robot ground rail z 240–480 and the cable-chain trough ROBOT_ZINCIR_OLUGU (on the floor, y 0–57, z 485–575, x 936–5100) are between the machine and the QR.\n\nOWNER DECISION (Kemal, today): NOTHING may be embedded below the floor (no part with y < 0). Cables run above the floor, between the feet of cabinets; enter the QR low through a side/front entry; nothing gets raised.\n\nYOUR SCOPE (two files only):\n1) Create h3/h3_ray_ek_v2.py as a copy of h3/h3_ray_ek_v1.py (keep its contract: kur(), PARCALAR, dunya(p), BIRIMLER, BIRIM_MODUL, ON_BIRIMLER, MALZEME, RZ, RX_MONTAJ, RAY_X, XF, L_ZINCIR, x_min_etkin(), kablo_hesabi(), etc.) and change it so that:\n   - the in-floor ZEMIN_KANALI parts (kanal_tabani, kanal_yan_*, kanal_uc_*, kanal_ayirici, kanal_kapagi_*) are removed;\n   - the robot cable (uzatma_A / uzatma_B / konnektör / kangal, Ø20, connector Ø26) stays inside the floor trough (oluk) up to x ≈ 5090, leaves the trough through its corridor-side wall (z 573–575) into a short COVERED floor bridge duct (304 sheet, same height class as the trough, sitting on the floor y ≥ 0, from z 575 to the QR face z 668) and enters the QR through a gland/cable-entry in a new kick plate at x ≈ 5090, y ≈ 25–75; inside the QR it goes to the existing kangal (coil) region / robot control box. No y < 0 anywhere. Update cable length bookkeeping (kablo_hesabi, kangal turns) consistently. Bump the docstring (v2, 1 Eki 2026, reason).\n2) Edit h3/h3_elk_qr_v1.py (the QR electrical layer; it already DUSURs and replaces the old main panel — use the same DUSUR/ekle/DELIKLER mechanism) so that:\n   - a fixed KICK PLATE (304 1,5, x 4572–5428, y 21–81, at the door plane) is added and the lower service door is replaced by a shortened door starting at y 84 (3 mm gap) — DUSUR the original `servis_kapagi_alt` (and any of its hinge/lock parts that would then clash or float) and add the new door/hinge parts at the right heights with BOM lines;\n   - the old floor entry (qr_guc_taban_rakoru_M40, the floor extension parts, anything going down through the base plate into the floor) is removed and replaced by TWO entries in the kick plate: (a) robot cable at x ≈ 5090 (split cable entry plate that passes a pre-assembled connector, e.g. icotek KEL-DP / KEL-QUICK or Murrelektronik Cable Entry — give a real catalog part no.), (b) the main power + data trunk to the machine at x ≈ 5395, y ≈ 25–75 (gland/entry sized for the cables that previously left the QR downward; read the file to see which cables those are — they currently run qr_alt_dikey_kanal / qr_alt_taban_kanali → floor). Re-route those cables inside the QR from the existing internal channels to entry (b) (channel/duct at the QR bottom, above the base plate, avoiding the kangal x 5107–5381 y 16–243 z 687–963, the robot control box x 4595–5070 y 20–443 z 675–943, UPS, etc.). Outside the QR, ANOTHER agent will bring a floor duct from entry (b) going toward −z along x 5370–5420 (top y ≤ 60): just leave the cable ends 30 mm outside the kick plate at x 5395, z 650, y 45 and print/document that interface point.\n   - Use real catalog parts (manufacturer + order no.) for glands/entries; cable diameters: Cat6A industrial Lapp ETHERLINE Cat.6A 2170465 Ø8.7; H07RN-F 3G2,5 Lapp 1600118 Ø≈12; ÖLFLEX CLASSIC 110 3G1,5 1119303 Ø6.7.\nDo NOT edit any other files (no h3_elk_hat_v1.py, h3_elk_ist_v1.py, h3_elektrik_v1.py, montaj/yap files, topping files). Do NOT run hat3_montaj_*.py or h3_elektrik_v1.py.\n\nVERIFY: (1) run h3_ray_ek_v2's self-check; (2) write a small script that loads the existing world dump B\\h3\\_dunya_tam\\dunya.brep + dunya.json (a compound; children order = json entries [birim, ad, mal, grup]) and checks every new/changed part of yours (build them by calling your module code; for h3_elk_qr_v1 you may need to call its kur(ekle, DELIKLER, DUSUR, QR) with a simple collector — read h3/h3_elektrik_v1.py to see how it is called) for real solid intersections (> 0.3 mm³) against the world, ignoring the parts you DUSUR and the QR parts you intentionally cut (list holes you need as DELIKLER entries). Also assert no part has y < 0. Report remaining contacts honestly.\n\nRETURN a concise report (Turkish OK): parts removed/added (names + bbox), the interface point for entry (b), catalog part numbers used, DELIKLER you added, check results, open issues. Don't paste whole files."},"uuid":"6fc406aa-4ca8-4218-9be1-d01be8e233d2","timestamp":"2026-10-01T12:50:23.935Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
